### API USAGE GUIDE
### ----------------------------------------------------
### PREREQUISITES:
### 1. Install "REST Client" extension in VS Code.
### 2. Make sure your server is running (`npm run dev` or `npm run start`).
### 3. Replace the `@token` variable below with a valid JWT token. 
###    (For Admin endpoints, make sure the JWT payload has { "role": "ADMIN" })

### Prerequisites Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api
@token = YOUR_VALID_JWT_TOKEN
@categoryId = REPLACE_WITH_CATEGORY_ID
@productId = REPLACE_WITH_PRODUCT_ID
@userId = REPLACE_WITH_USER_ID
@companyId = REPLACE_WITH_COMPANY_ID

### ====================================================
### 🔐 AUTH APIs
### ====================================================

### 1. Register User
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 2. Login User
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 3. Logout User
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 4. Forgot Password
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com"
}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 5. Reset Password
# Pass your OTP directly into the body here
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password/YOUR_OTP_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "otp": "123456",
  "password": "NewPassword123"
}

### ====================================================
### 📦 CATEGORY APIs
### ====================================================

### 1. Create Category [ADMIN]
# Requires: name (string, required)
# Response: 201 Created with category object
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Electronics"
}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 2. List Categories [PUBLIC/USER]
# Supports optional queries: ?page=1&limit=10&search=electro&startDate=2024-01-01&endDate=2024-12-31
# Response: 200 OK with paginated categories array
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories?page=1&limit=10
Content-Type: application/json

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 3. Get Single Category [PUBLIC/USER]
# Requires: valid category ID (24-char hex)
# Response: 200 OK with category object or 404 if not found
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories/{{categoryId}}
Content-Type: application/json

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 4. Update Category [ADMIN]
# Requires: valid category ID, optional name
# Response: 200 OK with updated category object
PUT {{baseUrl}}/categories/{{categoryId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Home Appliances"
}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 5. Delete Category (Soft Delete) [ADMIN]
# Requires: valid category ID
# Response: 200 OK with success message
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/categories/{{categoryId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json


### ====================================================
### 📦 PRODUCT APIs
### ====================================================

### 1. Create Product [ADMIN]
# IMPORTANT: "categories" must be an array of valid Category ObjectId(s).
# "company" is required. "festivals", "price", "stock", "attributes" are optional.
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Samsung Galaxy S24",
  "categories": ["{{categoryId}}"],
  "company": "{{companyId}}",
  "festivals": [],
  "price": 999.99,
  "stock": 50,
  "attributes": {
    "color": "Black",
    "storage": "256GB"
  }
}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 2. List Products [PUBLIC/USER]
# Supports optional queries: ?page=1&limit=10&search=samsung&category=ID1,ID2&festivals=ID1,ID2&company=ID&startDate=2024-01-01&endDate=2024-12-31
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?page=1&limit=10
Content-Type: application/json

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 3. Get Single Product [PUBLIC/USER]
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 4. Update Product [ADMIN]
PUT {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Samsung Galaxy S24 Ultra",
  "categories": ["{{categoryId}}"],
  "company": "{{companyId}}",
  "festivals": [],
  "price": 1199.99,
  "stock": 30,
  "attributes": {
    "color": "Black",
    "storage": "512GB"
  }
}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 5. Delete Product (Soft Delete) [ADMIN]
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json


### ====================================================
### 👥 USER MANAGEMENT APIs [ADMIN ONLY]
### ====================================================

### 1. Create User [ADMIN]
# Creates a new user with hashed password
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Smith",
  "email": "jane@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123",
  "role": "USER"
}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 2. List All Users [ADMIN]
# Supports optional queries: ?page=1&limit=10&search=jane&role=USER&startDate=2024-01-01&endDate=2024-12-31
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 3. Get Single User [ADMIN]
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 4. Update User [ADMIN]
# Can update: name, email, role
# Cannot update password through this endpoint (use change-password instead)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Doe Smith",
  "role": "ADMIN"
}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 5. Delete User - Soft Delete [ADMIN]
# User data is preserved but marked as deleted
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 6. Change Password [AUTHENTICATED USER]
# Any authenticated user can change their own password
# Requires old password verification
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "oldPassword": "CurrentPassword123",
  "newPassword": "NewPassword456"
}

### 📦 SECTION APIs
### ====================================================

### 1. Create Section [ADMIN]
# Requires: type ("banner"|"grid"|"horizontal_list", required), title (string, optional), dataSource (object, required), items (array, conditional)
# Response: 201 Created with section object
# Example Response:
# {
#   "_id": "6630f5b8...",
#   "type": "grid",
#   "title": "Summer Collection",
#   "status": "draft",
#   "isActive": true,
#   "displayOrder": 0,
#   "priority": 0,
#   "dataSource": { "type": "static" },
#   "columns": 2,
#   "items": [
#     { "image": "https://url.to/img.png", "cta": { "type": "category", "value": "ID" } }
#   ],
#   "createdAt": "2026-04-30T10:00:00.000Z",
#   "updatedAt": "2026-04-30T10:00:00.000Z"
# }
POST {{baseUrl}}/sections
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "grid",
  "title": "Summer Collection",
  "columns": 2,
  "dataSource": { "type": "static" },
  "items": [
    {
      "image": "https://example.com/summer-img1.png",
      "cta": { "type": "category", "value": "{{categoryId}}" }
    }
  ]
}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 2. List Sections [PUBLIC/USER]
# Supports optional queries: ?page=1&limit=10&search=summer
# Response: 200 OK with paginated sections array
# Example Response:
# {
#   "data": [
#     {
#       "_id": "6630f5b8a1e2c3d4e5f6a7b8",
#       "type": "grid",
#       "title": "Shop by Category",
#       "status": "published",
#       "isActive": true,
#       "displayOrder": 1,
#       "priority": 10,
#       "festival": "{{festivalId}}",
#       "dataSource": { "type": "static" },
#       "columns": 3,
#       "items": [
#         {
#           "image": "https://cdn.example.com/electronics.png",
#           "cta": { "type": "category", "value": "60d5ecb8b392d70015345671" }
#         },
#         {
#           "image": "https://cdn.example.com/fashion.png",
#           "cta": { "type": "category", "value": "60d5ecb8b392d70015345672" }
#         }
#       ],
#       "createdAt": "2026-04-30T10:00:00.000Z",
#       "updatedAt": "2026-04-30T10:00:00.000Z"
#     },
#     {
#       "_id": "6630f5c9b2e3d4f5a6b7c8d9",
#       "type": "banner",
#       "title": "Flash Sale",
#       "status": "published",
#       "isActive": true,
#       "displayOrder": 0,
#       "priority": 100,
#       "dataSource": { "type": "static" },
#       "items": [
#         {
#           "image": "https://cdn.example.com/banner1.png",
#           "cta": { "type": "product", "value": "60d5ecb8b392d70015345680" }
#         }
#       ],
#       "createdAt": "2026-04-30T09:00:00.000Z",
#       "updatedAt": "2026-04-30T09:30:00.000Z"
#     }
#   ],
#   "meta": {
#     "total": 2,
#     "page": 1,
#     "limit": 10,
#     "totalPages": 1
#   }
# }
GET {{baseUrl}}/sections?page=1&limit=10
Content-Type: application/json

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 3. Get Single Section [PUBLIC/USER]
# Requires: valid section ID (24-char hex)
# Response: 200 OK with section object or 404 if not found
# Example Response:
# {
#   "_id": "6630f5b8a1e2c3d4e5f6a7b8",
#   "type": "grid",
#   "title": "Shop by Category",
#   "status": "published",
#   "isActive": true,
#   "displayOrder": 1,
#   "priority": 10,
#   "dataSource": { "type": "static" },
#   "columns": 3,
#   "items": [
#     {
#       "image": "https://cdn.example.com/electronics.png",
#       "cta": { "type": "category", "value": "60d5ecb8b392d70015345671" }
#     },
#     {
#       "image": "https://cdn.example.com/fashion.png",
#       "cta": { "type": "category", "value": "60d5ecb8b392d70015345672" }
#     }
#   ],
#   "createdAt": "2026-04-30T10:00:00.000Z",
#   "updatedAt": "2026-04-30T10:00:00.000Z"
# }
GET {{baseUrl}}/sections/{{sectionId}}
Content-Type: application/json

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 4. Update Section [ADMIN]
# Requires: valid section ID, optional fields to update (e.g., title, status, isActive, items)
# Response: 200 OK with updated section object (same JSON structure as Create response)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/sections/{{sectionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated Summer Collection",
  "status": "published",
  "displayOrder": 1
}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 5. Delete Section (Hard Delete) [ADMIN]
# Requires: valid section ID
# Response: 200 OK with success message
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/sections/{{sectionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

